# Merge borders (reference/components/table.md#merged-borders), in the three tables from a rule For element: Table.
# Page area of 260 × 160 from (20, 20). Every cell has
# Padding: 2 and Border: 1 in #333333 and holds a block 20 high, so each row measures 24 plus the room its cells leave
# for the lines: half of the line between two cells, or the whole border on the edge of the table.
#
# t1: columns of 100 at x = 20 and 120. The header cells (style head) have a bottom border of 2 in #C00000, which wins
#   against the top border of 1 of the body: the line between them is 2 wide, centered on the line between the rows.
#   b1 takes up the two rows of the body: there is no line between them in its column.
#   Rows: header 1 + 24 + 1 = 26; first of the body 1 + 24 + 0.5 = 25.5; second 0.5 + 24 + 1 = 25.5.
# t2: four rows with Split rows: false; the fourth does not fit and moves to page 2. The line between the third and
#   the fourth row is drawn at the bottom of page 1 and at the top of page 2, inside the table on both.
#   Rows: 25.5, 25, 25, 25.5.
# t3: columns of 60. t3a has its border in #1F6FB2, t3b none and t3c a bottom border of 3. The line between t3a and
#   t3b is that of t3a; between t3b and t3c, that of t3c. The row measures what t3c does: 1 + 24 + 3 = 28.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: es
	Title: Prueba
	Page:
		Width: 300
		Height: 200
		Margin: 20
	Styles:
		For element: Document
			Typography:
				Font: IBM Plex Sans
				Size: 10
		For element: Cell
			Box:
				Padding: 2
				Border: 1
				Border color: #333333
		For element: Table
			Box:
				Merge borders: true
		For element: Block
			Box:
				Height: 20
				Background: #B5D4F4
		For style: head
			Box:
				Border: 1 1 2 1
				Border color: #C00000
	Section:
		Table:
			Id: t1
			Column sizes: 100 100
			Header rows:
				Row:
					Style: head
					Cell:
						Id: h1
						Block:
					Cell:
						Id: h2
						Block:
			Body:
				Row:
					Cell:
						Id: b1
						Span: 2 1
						Block:
					Cell:
						Id: b2
						Block:
				Row:
					Cell:
						Id: b3
						Block:
		Table:
			Id: t2
			Column sizes: 100 100
			Split rows: false
			Body:
				Row:
					Cell:
						Id: t2r1
						Block:
					Cell:
						Block:
				Row:
					Cell:
						Id: t2r2
						Block:
					Cell:
						Block:
				Row:
					Cell:
						Id: t2r3
						Block:
					Cell:
						Block:
				Row:
					Cell:
						Id: t2r4
						Block:
					Cell:
						Block:
		Table:
			Id: t3
			Column sizes: 60 60 60
			Body:
				Row:
					Cell:
						Id: t3a
						Box:
							Border color: #1F6FB2
						Block:
					Cell:
						Id: t3b
						Box:
							Border: 0
						Block:
					Cell:
						Id: t3c
						Box:
							Border: 1 1 3 1
						Block:
